 "quran": {
  "_about": "Ayat al-Quran on a card (Wan, 16 Nov 2026: 'make sure can write ayat al-Quran for reminder or under fatwa'). ONE copy, read by the page (web/src/lib/compliance.js, quran.js) and the worker (backend/semasa/compliance.py, quran.py). THE VERSE IS NEVER TYPED BY A WRITER, HUMAN OR AI: a slide names it by surah:ayat and the Arabic and the translation are fetched from a published source. `surahs` is [name, number of ayat] for surah 1 to 114, the names as quran.com writes them and the counts agreed by quran.com and alquran.cloud on 16 Nov 2026 (6,236 ayat). `max_span` is the most ayat one slide may carry. `editions` is the translation per stream, by its alquran.cloud identifier, with the same translation's id at quran.com, the credit drawn under the verse, and `sources`, the order the two sources are asked for the TRANSLATION. Basmeih is word for word the same at both (66 ayat compared on 16 Nov 2026). Saheeh International is not: quran.com carries the revised edition (\"lightning\" where alquran.cloud still has \"lightening\", 13:12), so English asks quran.com first. The ARABIC always prefers alquran.cloud (the Tanzil text) and, whenever both sources answered, the two are compared letter for letter and a verse they disagree on is refused. `bismillah` is the line alquran.cloud prefixes to ayat 1 of every surah but Al-Fatihah (where it IS ayat 1) and At-Tawbah (which has none): it is removed, because it is not part of that ayat.",
  "max_span": 3,
  "arabic": {
   "edition": "quran-uthmani",
   "credit": "Tanzil (Uthmani)"
  },
